From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 03:10:04 +0900
Subject: freedreno/drm: KGSL backend for the gallium driver

Upstream builds freedreno gallium for msm and virtio only ("the freedreno gallium driver doesn't
support KGSL", meson.options). On an Android kernel the Adreno GPU is /dev/kgsl-3d0 (Qualcomm
KGSL), not a DRM device, so GL there needs a KGSL backend for libfreedreno_drm.

The backend is upstream's closed MR !21570 (Hazematman) as carried by lfdevs/mesa-for-android-
container at 98f3d622, with its dma-buf allocation from /dev/dma_heap/system (ION as fallback)
and its reset-status query (FD_FEATURE_DIRECT_RESET), plus the branch's later fix 91f7e8c6f
(keep merged submits alive until the GPU command ioctl has consumed them) and a NULL check made
before use in kgsl_bo_new(). fd_device_new() takes a fd with no DRM version as KGSL. Left out:
the branch's control_fd/FD_FORCE_KGSL redirection, which is for systems that hand GBM a display
controller's DRM node; there is none here.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-30
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [!21570 was closed upstream; carried]
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:gpu.gl (FD710 renderer in KWin, plasmashell, glxinfo, glmark2)
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/research/94
